## What I checked

I read the brief and applied Daniel's bar. I opened the nine color prints and the nine line prints.
I compared each line file with its color file. I used the five pictures in `refs/` for the cast looks.
I counted every pixel that is not 0 and not 255 in all eighteen line files.
I measured the stroke depth in every line print. I measured the width of the narrow white areas.
I measured how far the cover objects reach into the top 30 percent band.

## Line file count

The count is 0 in all eighteen line files. No gray, no specks, no shading.
The nine line prints pass the writer check in the brief.

## Thick ring and band

A stroke wider than 40 px would show up in my depth scan. No such stroke exists in any line print.
The only solid black areas are the eye pupils. The deepest pupil measures 63 px from its centre to its edge.
The sun circle on the cover and the eye rings keep one even width.
So the stage 2 finding about a thick solid black ring or band is gone on every page.

## Narrow white areas

The narrow closed areas sit between two parallel strokes of the play equipment.
The narrowest one measures 2 px and the rest measure 5 to 14 px.
No narrow area sits inside a face or a hand. A child can color these areas or leave them white.
So no line gap makes the coloring hard.

## Cover row

The goal holds. Ben and Nan stand at the foot of the tall slide and both look up.
The low climbing frame stands at the far left. The round log beam lies left of centre.
The tall slide stands at the right. The sky, the clouds and the sun make a sunny playground.
Nan's cast look holds. Her two bunches have red ties, her shirt is orange with a white star,
her shorts are red, her shoes are white, her eyes are large and dark brown, and her eyelash mark shows.
No text shows in either file.

Top band: the slide tower posts reach 15 percent of the page height in the right quarter.
So the tower covers 15 points of the top 30 percent band. The left 60 percent of the band is empty sky.
The line art also draws a sun circle whose top sits at 3.5 percent of the height at the far right.
I judged the tower not a defect under the bar. The tower is the goal prop and the children look up at it.

Minor notes for the builder, none a defect:
- The line art puts a small mark at the outer corner of Ben's left eye. The color file has none.
  The mark measures 37 by 42 px on the 4000 px print. A mark of that size is not a defect under the bar.
- The line art draws a hard sun circle and a cloud at the top right. The color file shows a soft glow there.
- The line art draws a tree at the right edge. The color file has no tree there. The tree covers nothing.
- The climbing frame at the far left is cut by the page edge in both files.

