### C1, the nose page

The text is "A nose." The goal says that Nan touches her own nose with one finger and laughs.
The color file shows this. The nose sits between the eyes and the mouth, and the fingertip touches it.
Nan laughs with an open mouth. Her cast look holds in the color file.
The line art fails on its own subject. The fingertip rises to the place of the nose and then joins the mouth outline.
No nose shape shows between the eyes and the mouth. So the named face part does not show.
This is the stage 2 finding R13, and it stays in this file.
The line file holds 0 pixels outside 0 and 255. No stroke is wider than 40 px.
So the defect sits in the face alone, and the category is broken-face.

### C2, the nut page

The text is "A nut." The goal says that one big brown nut sits in Nan's open hand, close up.
Both files show this. One nut rests in her open palm, and the nut fills the left of the picture.
The nut has a dark brown cap, a tan body, a point at the bottom and a stem at the top in both files.
Nan's cast look holds. Her bunches have red ties, her shirt is orange with a white star, and her eyes are large and dark brown.
Each hand shows four fingers and one thumb in both files.
The line file holds 0 pixels outside 0 and 255. No stroke is wider than 40 px.
One note that is not a defect: the line art draws a ring pupil and a small highlight in each eye.

### C3, the practice line for the nose

The text is "nose". The goal says that the head of Nan is in profile facing the other way,
with the nose clearly seen, for a tracing practice line.
Both files show the head in profile. The nose stands clear in the profile outline.
The check row for the same word shows the head facing left. This page faces right, so the direction is the other way.
The line art is a closed outline that a child can trace. The eye has a solid pupil and a lash mark.
The line file holds 0 pixels outside 0 and 255. No stroke is wider than 40 px apart from the eye pupil.
Two notes that are not defects: the line art draws the hair bunch as a plain circle without the tie band,
and a white speck of 12 by 3 px sits inside the black hair mass at the top of the head.

